IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`
IMPORT `coa-definitions`

-- coa1-part3-constitution.l4: Part 3 of the Companies Act 2006 (United Kingdom), A company's constitution, ss 17 to 38
-- (lines 222-424 of ukpga-2006-46.txt). Layer 1: the law, objectively; every rule cites its provision with @ref and quotes the
-- text on `-- src:` lines (generated from the raw file by srcrefs.py quote). See the header of coa1-part2-formation.l4 for how to
-- read JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE and NOTHING and for the two kinds of function ("requirement met" and "the duty arises").
--
-- SOURCE. A plain-text rendering of the Act from legislation.gov.uk (Open Government Licence v3.0) made by a converter script;
-- it is not the official text and nothing here is "verified against the official text".
--
-- PENALTIES. The pounds a "level on the standard scale" stands for are not in the Act: each fine function takes them as an input.
-- Every NOT is bracketed: `NOT a OR b` reads as `NOT (a OR b)` on the stable binary.
-- Days are counted with `Day` (a date's day number); a period the text fixes ("not later than 15 days after ...") is tested at both ends.

-- =========================================================================================================
-- PART 3: A COMPANY'S CONSTITUTION (lines 222-424)
-- =========================================================================================================

-- ---- s 17: A company's constitution ----------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:224 | 17 A company's constitution
-- src:225 | Unless the context otherwise requires, references in the Companies Acts to a company's constitution include—
-- src:226 | (a) the company's articles, and
-- src:227 | (b) any resolutions and agreements to which Chapter 3 applies (see section 29).
@ref s 17 A company's constitution (src:224-227)
GIVEN `the context otherwise requires` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document is the company's articles` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 29 Chapter 3 applies to the resolution or agreement` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 17 the document is part of the company's constitution` MEANS
    IF `the context otherwise requires`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Unless the context otherwise requires"
    ELSE IF `the document is the company's articles`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE CONSIDER `s 29 Chapter 3 applies to the resolution or agreement`
              WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
              WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "references in the Companies Acts to a company's constitution include— (a) the company's articles, and (b) any resolutions and agreements to which Chapter 3 applies"
              WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether Chapter 3 applies is s 29's answer

-- ---- s 18: Articles of association -----------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:230 | 18 Articles of association
-- src:231 | (1) A company must have articles of association prescribing regulations for the company.
@ref s 18(1) Articles of association: a company must have articles (src:230-231)
GIVEN `the company has articles of association prescribing regulations for the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 18(1) the company has articles of association as required` MEANS
    IF `the company has articles of association prescribing regulations for the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A company must have articles of association prescribing regulations for the company" (a bare "must" not done, fork F-C1)

-- src:232 | (2) Unless it is a company to which model articles apply by virtue of section 20 (default application of model articles in case of limited company), it must register articles of association.
@ref s 18(2) Articles of association: registering articles unless model articles apply (src:232-232)
GIVEN liability IS A `Liability of members`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 18(2) the company must register articles of association` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 3(1) the company is a limited company` liability
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Unless it is a company to which model articles apply by virtue of section 20 (default application of model articles in case of limited company), it must register articles of association"
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): follows s 3(1)

DECLARE `s 18(2) action` IS ONE OF
    `s 18(2) register articles of association with the registrar`

@ref s 18(2) Articles of association: registering articles unless model articles apply (src:232-232)
GIVEN liability IS A `Liability of members`
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 18(2) action`
`s 18(2) the company's duty to register articles` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 18(2) the company must register articles of association` liability
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        PARTY Company
        MUST `s 18(2) register articles of association with the registrar`
        HENCE FULFILLED
        LEST BREACH BY Company BECAUSE "the company is not a company to which model articles apply by virtue of section 20 and did not register articles of association"
    OTHERWISE FULFILLED

-- src:233 | (3) Articles of association registered by a company must—
-- src:234 | (a) be contained in a single document, and
-- src:235 | (b) be divided into paragraphs numbered consecutively.
@ref s 18(3) Articles of association: the form of registered articles (src:233-235)
GIVEN `the registered articles are contained in a single document` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the registered articles are divided into paragraphs numbered consecutively` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 18(3) the registered articles meet the requirements as to form` MEANS
    IF `the registered articles are contained in a single document` AND `the registered articles are divided into paragraphs numbered consecutively`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Articles of association registered by a company must— (a) be contained in a single document, and (b) be divided into paragraphs numbered consecutively" (a bare "must" not done, fork F-C1)

-- src:236 | (4) References in the Companies Acts to a company's “articles” are to its articles of association.
@ref s 18(4) Articles of association: the meaning of "articles" (src:236-236)
GIVEN `the document is the company's articles of association` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 18(4) the reference in the Companies Acts is to the company's articles of association` MEANS
    IF `the document is the company's articles of association`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "References in the Companies Acts to a company's “articles” are to its articles of association"

-- ---- s 19: Power of Secretary of State to prescribe model articles ---------------------------------------
-- s 19(1) (the power), s 19(2) (different model articles for different descriptions) and s 19(5) (negative resolution procedure)
-- are regulation-making machinery: inert under reason 2. s 19(3) and (4) are operative for a company.

-- src:240 | (3) A company may adopt all or any of the provisions of model articles.
@ref s 19(3) Power to prescribe model articles: a company may adopt model articles (src:240-240)
GIVEN `the company adopts all or any of the provisions of model articles` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 19(3) the company may adopt the provisions of model articles` MEANS
    IF `the company adopts all or any of the provisions of model articles`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A company may adopt all or any of the provisions of model articles"

-- src:241 | (4) Any amendment of model articles by regulations under this section does not affect a company registered before the amendment takes effect.
-- src:242 | “Amendment” here includes addition, alteration or repeal.
@ref s 19(4) Power to prescribe model articles: amendment does not affect a company registered before (src:241-242)
GIVEN `the company was registered before the amendment of the model articles takes effect` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 19(4) an amendment of the model articles affects the company` MEANS
    IF `the company was registered before the amendment of the model articles takes effect`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Any amendment of model articles by regulations under this section does not affect a company registered before the amendment takes effect"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence speaks only of "a company registered before the amendment takes effect"

@ref s 19(4) Power to prescribe model articles: "Amendment" includes addition, alteration or repeal (src:242-242)
GIVEN `the change is an addition` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the change is an alteration` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the change is a repeal` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 19(4) the change to the model articles is an amendment` MEANS
    IF `the change is an addition` OR `the change is an alteration` OR `the change is a repeal`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "“Amendment” here includes addition, alteration or repeal"

-- ---- s 20: Default application of model articles ---------------------------------------------------------

-- src:244 | 20 Default application of model articles
-- src:245 | (1) On the formation of a limited company—
-- src:246 | (a) if articles are not registered, or
-- src:247 | (b) if articles are registered, in so far as they do not exclude or modify the relevant model articles,
-- src:248 | the relevant model articles (so far as applicable) form part of the company's articles in the same manner and to the same extent as if articles in the form of those articles had been duly registered.
@ref s 20(1) Default application of model articles: the relevant model articles form part of the articles (src:244-248)
GIVEN liability IS A `Liability of members`
      `articles are registered` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the registered articles exclude or modify the provision of the relevant model articles` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provision of the relevant model articles is applicable to the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 20(1) the provision of the relevant model articles forms part of the company's articles` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 3(1) the company is a limited company` liability
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): follows s 3(1)
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "On the formation of a limited company— ... the relevant model articles ... form part of the company's articles" ("on" counts as "where", ruling of 2026-11-05 (c))
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF NOT `the provision of the relevant model articles is applicable to the company`
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the relevant model articles (so far as applicable) form part of the company's articles"
        ELSE IF NOT `articles are registered`
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE IF `the registered articles exclude or modify the provision of the relevant model articles`
                  THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if articles are registered, in so far as they do not exclude or modify the relevant model articles"
                  ELSE JUST TRUE

DECLARE `s 20(2) version of the model articles` HAS
    `date the version took effect` IS A DATE
    `name of the version` IS A STRING

-- src:249 | (2) The “relevant model articles” means the model articles prescribed for a company of that description as in force at the date on which the company is registered.
@ref s 20(2) Default application of model articles: the relevant model articles (src:249-249)
GIVEN `the date on which the company is registered` IS A DATE
      versions IS A LIST OF `s 20(2) version of the model articles`
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`s 20(2) the relevant model articles` MEANS
    CONSIDER best
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): no version of the model articles was in force at the date on which the company is registered
    WHEN JUST v THEN JUST (v's `name of the version`)
    WHERE
        eligible MEANS filter (GIVEN v YIELD v's `date the version took effect` AT MOST `the date on which the company is registered`) versions
        best MEANS foldr pick NOTHING eligible
        pick x acc MEANS
            CONSIDER acc
            WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST x
            WHEN JUST a THEN IF x's `date the version took effect` AT LEAST a's `date the version took effect` THEN JUST x ELSE JUST a

-- ---- s 21: Amendment of articles -------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:251 | 21 Amendment of articles
-- src:252 | (1) A company may amend its articles by special resolution.
@ref s 21(1) Amendment of articles: by special resolution (src:251-252)
GIVEN `s 283 the resolution is a special resolution` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 21(1) the company may amend its articles by the resolution` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 283 the resolution is a special resolution`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A company may amend its articles by special resolution" (other routes, such as agreement of all the members, are not excluded: s 22(3))
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether a resolution is a special resolution is s 283's answer

DECLARE `s 21 enactment the power to amend is subject to` IS ONE OF
    `s 21 sections 197 and 198 of the Charities Act 2011`
    `s 21 section 96 of the Charities Act (Northern Ireland) 2008`
    `s 21 section 112 of the Companies Act 1989`
    `s 21 section 16 of the Charities and Trustee Investment (Scotland) Act 2005`

-- src:253 | (2) In the case of a company that is a charity, this is subject to—
-- src:254 | (a) in England and Wales, sections 197 and 198 of the Charities Act 2011;
-- src:255 | (b) in Northern Ireland, section 96 of the Charities Act (Northern Ireland) 2008 .
-- src:256 | (3) In the case of a company that is registered in the Scottish Charity Register, this is subject to—
-- src:257 | (a) section 112 of the Companies Act 1989 (c. 40), and
-- src:258 | (b) section 16 of the Charities and Trustee Investment (Scotland) Act 2005 (asp 10).
@ref s 21(2) and (3) Amendment of articles: charities (src:253-258)
GIVEN `the company is a charity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is registered in the Scottish Charity Register` IS A BOOLEAN
      place IS A `Place of registration`
GIVETH A LIST OF `s 21 enactment the power to amend is subject to`
`s 21(2) and (3) the enactments the power to amend articles is subject to` MEANS
    concat (LIST charityEW, charityNI, scottish)
    WHERE
        charityEW MEANS IF `the company is a charity` AND place EQUALS `England and Wales` THEN LIST `s 21 sections 197 and 198 of the Charities Act 2011` ELSE EMPTY
        charityNI MEANS IF `the company is a charity` AND place EQUALS `Northern Ireland` THEN LIST `s 21 section 96 of the Charities Act (Northern Ireland) 2008` ELSE EMPTY
        scottish MEANS IF `the company is registered in the Scottish Charity Register` THEN LIST `s 21 section 112 of the Companies Act 1989`, `s 21 section 16 of the Charities and Trustee Investment (Scotland) Act 2005` ELSE EMPTY
    -- An empty list is the text's own "no" ("In the case of a company that is a charity, this is subject to ..."; "In the case of a company that is registered in the Scottish Charity Register, this is subject to ..."): FALSE-kind, "where" (ruling of 2026-11-05 (b)).

-- ---- s 22: Entrenched provisions of the articles ---------------------------------------------------------

-- src:259 | 22 Entrenched provisions of the articles
-- src:260 | (1) A company's articles may contain provision (“provision for entrenchment”) to the effect that specified provisions of the articles may be amended or repealed only if conditions are met, or procedures are complied with, that are more restrictive than those applicable in the case of a special resolution.
@ref s 22(1) Entrenched provisions of the articles: provision for entrenchment (src:259-260)
GIVEN `the provision specifies provisions of the articles that may be amended or repealed only if conditions are met or procedures are complied with` IS A BOOLEAN
      `those conditions or procedures are more restrictive than those applicable in the case of a special resolution` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 22(1) the provision is provision for entrenchment` MEANS
    IF `the provision specifies provisions of the articles that may be amended or repealed only if conditions are met or procedures are complied with` AND `those conditions or procedures are more restrictive than those applicable in the case of a special resolution`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(“provision for entrenchment”) to the effect that specified provisions of the articles may be amended or repealed only if conditions are met, or procedures are complied with, that are more restrictive than those applicable in the case of a special resolution"

-- src:261 | (2) Provision for entrenchment may only be made—
-- src:262 | (a) in the company's articles on formation, or
-- src:263 | (b) by an amendment of the company's articles agreed to by all the members of the company.
@ref s 22(2) Entrenched provisions of the articles: when it may be made (src:261-263)
GIVEN `the provision is made in the company's articles on formation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provision is made by an amendment of the company's articles agreed to by all the members of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 22(2) provision for entrenchment may be made` MEANS
    IF `the provision is made in the company's articles on formation` OR `the provision is made by an amendment of the company's articles agreed to by all the members of the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Provision for entrenchment may only be made— (a) in the company's articles on formation, or (b) by an amendment of the company's articles agreed to by all the members of the company"

-- src:264 | (3) Provision for entrenchment does not prevent amendment of the company's articles—
-- src:265 | (a) by agreement of all the members of the company, or
-- src:266 | (b) by order of a court or other authority having power to alter the company's articles.
@ref s 22(3) Entrenched provisions of the articles: amendment that it does not prevent (src:264-266)
GIVEN `the amendment is by agreement of all the members of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amendment is by order of a court or other authority having power to alter the company's articles` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 22(3) provision for entrenchment prevents the amendment` MEANS
    IF `the amendment is by agreement of all the members of the company` OR `the amendment is by order of a court or other authority having power to alter the company's articles`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Provision for entrenchment does not prevent amendment of the company's articles— (a) by agreement of all the members of the company, or (b) by order of a court or other authority having power to alter the company's articles"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the flat negative names only agreement of all the members and an order of a court or other authority; any other amendment is governed by the provision for entrenchment itself

-- src:267 | (4) Nothing in this section affects any power of a court or other authority to alter a company's articles.
@ref s 22(4) Entrenched provisions of the articles: powers of a court or other authority (src:267-267)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 22(4) this section affects any power of a court or other authority to alter a company's articles` MEANS
    JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Nothing in this section affects any power of a court or other authority to alter a company's articles"

-- ---- s 23: Notice to registrar of existence of restriction on amendment of articles ----------------------

DECLARE `s 23 action` IS ONE OF
    `s 23(1) give the registrar notice that the articles contain, or are restricted by, provision for entrenchment`
    `s 23(2) give the registrar notice that provision for entrenchment or another restriction has been removed`

-- src:268 | 23 Notice to registrar of existence of restriction on amendment of articles
-- src:269 | (1) Where a company's articles—
-- src:270 | (a) on formation contain provision for entrenchment,
-- src:271 | (b) are amended so as to include such provision, or
-- src:272 | (c) are altered by order of a court or other authority so as to restrict or exclude the power of the company to amend its articles,
-- src:273 | the company must give notice of that fact to the registrar.
@ref s 23(1) Notice to registrar: restriction on amendment (src:268-273)
GIVEN `the articles on formation contain provision for entrenchment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the articles are amended so as to include provision for entrenchment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the articles are altered by order of a court or other authority so as to restrict or exclude the power of the company to amend its articles` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 23(1) the company must give notice to the registrar of the entrenchment or restriction` MEANS
    IF `the articles on formation contain provision for entrenchment` OR `the articles are amended so as to include provision for entrenchment` OR `the articles are altered by order of a court or other authority so as to restrict or exclude the power of the company to amend its articles`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a company's articles— (a) ..., (b) ..., or (c) ..., the company must give notice of that fact to the registrar" (the duty arises only where, ruling of 2026-11-05 (b))

@ref s 23(1) Notice to registrar: restriction on amendment (src:269-273)
GIVEN `the articles on formation contain provision for entrenchment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the articles are amended so as to include provision for entrenchment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the articles are altered by order of a court or other authority so as to restrict or exclude the power of the company to amend its articles` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 23 action`
`s 23(1) the company's duty to give notice of the restriction` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 23(1) the company must give notice to the registrar of the entrenchment or restriction` `the articles on formation contain provision for entrenchment` `the articles are amended so as to include provision for entrenchment` `the articles are altered by order of a court or other authority so as to restrict or exclude the power of the company to amend its articles`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        PARTY Company
        MUST `s 23(1) give the registrar notice that the articles contain, or are restricted by, provision for entrenchment`
        HENCE FULFILLED
        LEST BREACH BY Company BECAUSE "the company did not give the registrar notice of the provision for entrenchment or restriction"
    OTHERWISE FULFILLED

-- src:274 | (2) Where a company's articles—
-- src:275 | (a) are amended so as to remove provision for entrenchment, or
-- src:276 | (b) are altered by order of a court or other authority—
-- src:277 | (i) so as to remove such provision, or
-- src:278 | (ii) so as to remove any other restriction on, or any exclusion of, the power of the company to amend its articles,
-- src:279 | the company must give notice of that fact to the registrar.
@ref s 23(2) Notice to registrar: removal of restriction on amendment (src:274-279)
GIVEN `the articles are amended so as to remove provision for entrenchment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the articles are altered by order so as to remove provision for entrenchment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the articles are altered by order so as to remove any other restriction on, or exclusion of, the power of the company to amend its articles` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 23(2) the company must give notice to the registrar of the removal` MEANS
    IF `the articles are amended so as to remove provision for entrenchment` OR `the articles are altered by order so as to remove provision for entrenchment` OR `the articles are altered by order so as to remove any other restriction on, or exclusion of, the power of the company to amend its articles`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a company's articles— (a) ... or (b) ..., the company must give notice of that fact to the registrar" (the duty arises only where, ruling of 2026-11-05 (b))

@ref s 23(2) Notice to registrar: removal of restriction on amendment (src:274-279)
GIVEN `the articles are amended so as to remove provision for entrenchment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the articles are altered by order so as to remove provision for entrenchment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the articles are altered by order so as to remove any other restriction on, or exclusion of, the power of the company to amend its articles` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 23 action`
`s 23(2) the company's duty to give notice of the removal` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 23(2) the company must give notice to the registrar of the removal` `the articles are amended so as to remove provision for entrenchment` `the articles are altered by order so as to remove provision for entrenchment` `the articles are altered by order so as to remove any other restriction on, or exclusion of, the power of the company to amend its articles`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        PARTY Company
        MUST `s 23(2) give the registrar notice that provision for entrenchment or another restriction has been removed`
        HENCE FULFILLED
        LEST BREACH BY Company BECAUSE "the company did not give the registrar notice of the removal of provision for entrenchment or of another restriction"
    OTHERWISE FULFILLED

-- ---- s 24: Statement of compliance where amendment of articles restricted --------------------------------

-- src:280 | 24 Statement of compliance where amendment of articles restricted
-- src:281 | (1) This section applies where a company's articles are subject—
-- src:282 | (a) to provision for entrenchment, or
-- src:283 | (b) to an order of a court or other authority restricting or excluding the company's power to amend the articles.
@ref s 24(1) Statement of compliance: when the section applies (src:280-283)
GIVEN `the articles are subject to provision for entrenchment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the articles are subject to an order of a court or other authority restricting or excluding the company's power to amend the articles` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 24(1) this section applies` MEANS
    IF `the articles are subject to provision for entrenchment` OR `the articles are subject to an order of a court or other authority restricting or excluding the company's power to amend the articles`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies where a company's articles are subject— (a) to provision for entrenchment, or (b) to an order of a court or other authority restricting or excluding the company's power to amend the articles"

-- src:284 | (2) If the company—
-- src:285 | (a) amends its articles, and
-- src:286 | (b) is required to send to the registrar a document making or evidencing the amendment,
-- src:287 | the company must deliver with that document a statement of compliance.
@ref s 24(2) Statement of compliance: the duty to deliver it (src:284-287)
GIVEN `the answer under s 24(1) that this section applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the company amends its articles` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is required to send to the registrar a document making or evidencing the amendment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 24(2) the company must deliver a statement of compliance with the document` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the answer under s 24(1) that this section applies`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): follows s 24(1)
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies where ..." (s 24(1)): the duty arises only where the section applies
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF `the company amends its articles` AND `the company is required to send to the registrar a document making or evidencing the amendment`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the company— (a) amends its articles, and (b) is required to send to the registrar a document making or evidencing the amendment, the company must deliver with that document a statement of compliance"

DECLARE `s 24(2) action` IS ONE OF
    `s 24(2) deliver a statement of compliance with the document`

@ref s 24(2) Statement of compliance: the duty to deliver it (src:284-287)
GIVEN `the section applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the company amends its articles` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is required to send to the registrar a document making or evidencing the amendment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 24(2) action`
`s 24(2) the company's duty to deliver a statement of compliance` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 24(2) the company must deliver a statement of compliance with the document` `the section applies` `the company amends its articles` `the company is required to send to the registrar a document making or evidencing the amendment`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        PARTY Company
        MUST `s 24(2) deliver a statement of compliance with the document`
        HENCE FULFILLED
        LEST BREACH BY Company BECAUSE "the company did not deliver a statement of compliance with the document"
    OTHERWISE FULFILLED

-- src:288 | (3) The statement of compliance required is a statement certifying that the amendment has been made in accordance with the company's articles and, where relevant, any applicable order of a court or other authority.
@ref s 24(3) Statement of compliance: what it certifies (src:288-288)
GIVEN `the statement certifies that the amendment has been made in accordance with the company's articles` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an order of a court or other authority applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement certifies that the amendment has been made in accordance with the order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 24(3) the statement is the statement of compliance required` MEANS
    IF `the statement certifies that the amendment has been made in accordance with the company's articles` AND ((NOT `an order of a court or other authority applies`) OR `the statement certifies that the amendment has been made in accordance with the order`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The statement of compliance required is a statement certifying that the amendment has been made in accordance with the company's articles and, where relevant, any applicable order of a court or other authority"

-- src:289 | (4) The registrar may rely on the statement of compliance as sufficient evidence of the matters stated in it.
