GIVEN `the member agrees in writing, either before or after the alteration is made, to be bound by the alteration` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 25(2) subsection (1) applies to the member` MEANS
    IF `the member agrees in writing, either before or after the alteration is made, to be bound by the alteration`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (1) does not apply in a case where the member agrees in writing, either before or after the alteration is made, to be bound by the alteration"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): subsection (2) says only when subsection (1) does not apply; whether it applies is subsection (1)'s own wording

-- src:290 | 25 Effect of alteration of articles on company's members
-- src:291 | (1) A member of a company is not bound by an alteration to its articles after the date on which he became a member, if and so far as the alteration—
-- src:292 | (a) requires him to take or subscribe for more shares than the number held by him at the date on which the alteration is made, or
-- src:293 | (b) in any way increases his liability as at that date to contribute to the company's share capital or otherwise to pay money to the company.
@ref s 25(1) Effect of alteration of articles: a member is not bound by some alterations (src:290-293)
GIVEN `the alteration is made after the date on which he became a member` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of shares the alteration requires him to take or subscribe for` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of shares held by him at the date on which the alteration is made` IS A NUMBER
      `the alteration in any way increases his liability as at that date to contribute to the company's share capital or otherwise to pay money to the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the member agrees in writing to be bound by the alteration` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 25(1) the member is not bound by the alteration` MEANS
    IF `the member agrees in writing to be bound by the alteration`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): s 25(2) takes the case out of subsection (1) and the section does not say that the member is then bound
    ELSE IF NOT `the alteration is made after the date on which he became a member`
         THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an alteration to its articles after the date on which he became a member"
         ELSE IF `the number of shares the alteration requires him to take or subscribe for` GREATER THAN `the number of shares held by him at the date on which the alteration is made` OR `the alteration in any way increases his liability as at that date to contribute to the company's share capital or otherwise to pay money to the company`
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is not bound by an alteration ... if and so far as the alteration— (a) requires him to take or subscribe for more shares than the number held by him ..., or (b) in any way increases his liability" (a failed "if" read as the text's no, marginal reading (a))

-- ---- s 26: Registrar to be sent copy of amended articles -------------------------------------------------

-- src:295 | 26 Registrar to be sent copy of amended articles
-- src:296 | (1) Where a company amends its articles it must send to the registrar a copy of the articles as amended not later than 15 days after the amendment takes effect.
