    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section does not require a company to set out in its articles any provisions of model articles that— (a) are applied by the articles, or (b) apply by virtue of section 20"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the flat negative names only provisions applied by the articles or applying by virtue of s 20

-- src:300 | (3) If a company fails to comply with this section an offence is committed by—
-- src:301 | (a) the company, and
-- src:302 | (b) every officer of the company who is in default.
@ref s 26(3) Copy of amended articles: offence by the company (src:300-302)
GIVEN `the company fails to comply with section 26` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 26(3)(a) the company commits an offence` MEANS
    IF `the company fails to comply with section 26`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a company fails to comply with this section an offence is committed by— (a) the company" (a failed "if" read as the text's no, marginal reading (a))

@ref s 26(3) Copy of amended articles: offence by an officer in default (src:300-302)
GIVEN `the company fails to comply with section 26` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 1121 the officer is in default` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 26(3)(b) the officer of the company commits an offence` MEANS
    IF NOT `the company fails to comply with section 26`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a company fails to comply with this section an offence is committed by— ... (b) every officer of the company who is in default" (a failed "if" read as the text's no, marginal reading (a))
    ELSE CONSIDER `s 1121 the officer is in default`
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the offence is committed by "every officer of the company who is in default" and the text is silent on an officer who is not
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether an officer is in default is s 1121's answer

-- src:303 | (4) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding level 3 on the standard scale and, for continued contravention, a daily default fine not exceeding one-tenth of level 3 on the standard scale.
@ref s 26(4) Copy of amended articles: the penalty (src:303-303)
`s 26(4) the penalty` MEANS Penalty WITH
    `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction`
