    IF `it appears to the registrar that the company has failed to comply with an enactment requiring it to send a document making or evidencing an alteration in the company's articles` OR `it appears to the registrar that the company has failed to comply with an enactment requiring it to send a copy of the company's articles as amended`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): fork F42, a grant whose "if" is unmet (the other reading is JUST FALSE): "If it appears to the registrar that a company has failed to comply with any enactment requiring it— (a) ..., or (b) ..., the registrar may give notice to the company requiring it to comply"

