         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the offence is committed by "every officer of it who is in default" and the text is silent on an officer who is not
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether an officer is in default is s 1121's answer

-- src:335 | (3) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding level 3 on the standard scale and, for continued contravention, a daily default fine not exceeding one-tenth of level 3 on the standard scale.
@ref s 30(3) Copies of resolutions or agreements to be forwarded to registrar: the penalty (src:335-335)
`s 30(3) the penalty` MEANS Penalty WITH
    `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction`
    `imprisonment not exceeding` IS NOTHING
    `fine not exceeding` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 1)
    `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 0.1)
    `imprisonment and fine together` IS FALSE

@ref s 30(3) Copies of resolutions or agreements to be forwarded to registrar: the most the person can be fined (src:335-335)
GIVEN `level 3 on the standard scale, in pounds` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 30(3) the most the person can be fined on summary conviction, in pounds` MEANS
    `level 3 on the standard scale, in pounds`

@ref s 30(3) Copies of resolutions or agreements to be forwarded to registrar: the most the daily default fine can be (src:335-335)
GIVEN `level 3 on the standard scale, in pounds` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 30(3) the most the daily default fine can be for each day of continued contravention, in pounds` MEANS
    `level 3 on the standard scale, in pounds` TIMES 0.1

-- src:336 | (4) For the purposes of this section, a liquidator of the company is treated as an officer of it.
@ref s 30(4) Copies of resolutions or agreements to be forwarded to registrar: a liquidator is treated as an officer (src:336-336)
GIVEN `the person is a liquidator of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 30(4) the person is treated as an officer of the company for the purposes of section 30` MEANS
    IF `the person is a liquidator of the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "For the purposes of this section, a liquidator of the company is treated as an officer of it"

-- =========================================================================================================
-- CHAPTER 4: MISCELLANEOUS AND SUPPLEMENTARY PROVISIONS (lines 337-424)
-- =========================================================================================================

-- ---- s 31: Statement of company's objects ----------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:339 | 31 Statement of company's objects
-- src:340 | (1) Unless a company's articles specifically restrict the objects of the company, its objects are unrestricted.
@ref s 31(1) Statement of company's objects: unrestricted unless the articles restrict them (src:339-340)
GIVEN `the company's articles specifically restrict the objects of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 31(1) the company's objects are unrestricted` MEANS
    IF `the company's articles specifically restrict the objects of the company`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Unless a company's articles specifically restrict the objects of the company, its objects are unrestricted"
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:341 | (2) Where a company amends its articles so as to add, remove or alter a statement of the company's objects—
-- src:342 | (a) it must give notice to the registrar,
@ref s 31(2)(a) Statement of company's objects: notice to the registrar (src:341-342)
GIVEN `the company amends its articles so as to add, remove or alter a statement of the company's objects` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 31(2)(a) the company must give notice to the registrar` MEANS
    IF `the company amends its articles so as to add, remove or alter a statement of the company's objects`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a company amends its articles so as to add, remove or alter a statement of the company's objects— (a) it must give notice to the registrar" (the duty arises only where, ruling of 2026-11-05 (b))

-- src:343 | (b) on receipt of the notice, the registrar shall register it, and
@ref s 31(2)(b) Statement of company's objects: the registrar shall register the notice (src:343-343)
GIVEN `the registrar has received the notice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 31(2)(b) the registrar shall register the notice` MEANS
    IF `the registrar has received the notice`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "on receipt of the notice, the registrar shall register it" ("on receipt" counts as "where", ruling of 2026-11-05 (c))

-- src:344 | (c) the amendment is not effective until entry of that notice on the register.
@ref s 31(2)(c) Statement of company's objects: effective on entry of the notice on the register (src:344-344)
GIVEN `the notice has been entered on the register` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 31(2)(c) the amendment cannot yet be effective` MEANS
    IF `the notice has been entered on the register`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the amendment is not effective until entry of that notice on the register" (the bar ends on entry, ruling of 2026-11-05 (d); the function never claims that the amendment has become effective)
    ELSE JUST TRUE

DECLARE `s 31(2) action` IS ONE OF
    `s 31(2)(a) give the registrar notice of the amendment of the statement of the company's objects`
    `s 31(2)(b) register the notice`

-- src:341 | (2) Where a company amends its articles so as to add, remove or alter a statement of the company's objects—
-- src:342 | (a) it must give notice to the registrar,
-- src:343 | (b) on receipt of the notice, the registrar shall register it, and
-- src:344 | (c) the amendment is not effective until entry of that notice on the register.
@ref s 31(2) Statement of company's objects: the chain from notice to entry (src:341-344)
GIVEN `the company amends its articles so as to add, remove or alter a statement of the company's objects` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 31(2) action`
`s 31(2) the company's duty to give notice, and the registrar's duty to register it` MEANS
    IF `the company amends its articles so as to add, remove or alter a statement of the company's objects`
    THEN PARTY Company
         MUST `s 31(2)(a) give the registrar notice of the amendment of the statement of the company's objects`
         HENCE (PARTY Registrar
                MUST `s 31(2)(b) register the notice`
                HENCE FULFILLED
                LEST BREACH BY Registrar BECAUSE "on receipt of the notice the registrar did not register it")
         LEST BREACH BY Company BECAUSE "the company did not give the registrar notice of the amendment of its statement of objects"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- src:345 | (3) Any such amendment does not affect any rights or obligations of the company or render defective any legal proceedings by or against it.
@ref s 31(3) Statement of company's objects: the amendment does not affect rights or proceedings (src:345-345)
GIVEN `the amendment adds, removes or alters a statement of the company's objects` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 31(3) the amendment affects any rights or obligations of the company` MEANS
    IF `the amendment adds, removes or alters a statement of the company's objects`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Any such amendment does not affect any rights or obligations of the company"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any such amendment" is an amendment of the kind in subsection (2)

@ref s 31(3) Statement of company's objects: legal proceedings (src:345-345)
GIVEN `the amendment adds, removes or alters a statement of the company's objects` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 31(3) the amendment renders defective any legal proceedings by or against the company` MEANS
    IF `the amendment adds, removes or alters a statement of the company's objects`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Any such amendment does not ... render defective any legal proceedings by or against it"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any such amendment" is an amendment of the kind in subsection (2)

DECLARE `s 31 enactment the section is subject to` IS ONE OF
    `s 31 sections 197 and 198 of the Charities Act 2011`
    `s 31 section 96 of the Charities Act (Northern Ireland) 2008`
    `s 31 the provisions of the Charities and Trustee Investment (Scotland) Act 2005`

-- src:346 | (4) In the case of a company that is a charity, the provisions of this section have effect subject to—
-- src:347 | (a) in England and Wales, sections 197 and 198 of the Charities Act 2011;
-- src:348 | (b) in Northern Ireland, section 96 of the Charities Act (Northern Ireland) 2008 .
-- src:349 | (5) In the case of a company that is entered in the Scottish Charity Register, the provisions of this section have effect subject to the provisions of the Charities and Trustee Investment (Scotland) Act 2005 (asp 10).
@ref s 31(4) and (5) Statement of company's objects: charities (src:346-349)
GIVEN `the company is a charity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is entered in the Scottish Charity Register` IS A BOOLEAN
      place IS A `Place of registration`
GIVETH A LIST OF `s 31 enactment the section is subject to`
`s 31(4) and (5) the enactments this section has effect subject to` MEANS
    concat (LIST charityEW, charityNI, scottish)
    WHERE
        charityEW MEANS IF `the company is a charity` AND place EQUALS `England and Wales` THEN LIST `s 31 sections 197 and 198 of the Charities Act 2011` ELSE EMPTY
        charityNI MEANS IF `the company is a charity` AND place EQUALS `Northern Ireland` THEN LIST `s 31 section 96 of the Charities Act (Northern Ireland) 2008` ELSE EMPTY
        scottish MEANS IF `the company is entered in the Scottish Charity Register` THEN LIST `s 31 the provisions of the Charities and Trustee Investment (Scotland) Act 2005` ELSE EMPTY
    -- An empty list is the text's own "no" ("In the case of a company that is a charity ... subject to"; "In the case of a company that is entered in the Scottish Charity Register ... subject to"): FALSE-kind, "where" (ruling of 2026-11-05 (b)).

-- ---- s 32: Constitutional documents to be provided to members --------------------------------------------

DECLARE `s 32(1) document the company must send` IS ONE OF
    `s 32(1)(a) an up-to-date copy of the company's articles`
    `s 32(1)(b) a copy of a resolution or agreement to which Chapter 3 applies that is for the time being in force`
    `s 32(1)(c)(i) a copy of a document sent to the registrar under section 34(2)`
    `s 32(1)(c)(ii) a copy of a document sent to the registrar under section 35(2)(a)`
    `s 32(1)(d) a copy of a court order under section 899 or 900`
    `s 32(1)(da) a copy of a court order under section 901F or 901J`
    `s 32(1)(e) a copy of a court order under section 996 that alters the company's constitution`
    `s 32(1)(f) a copy of the company's current certificate of incorporation, and of any past certificates`
    `s 32(1)(g) a current statement of capital`
    `s 32(1)(h) a copy of the statement of guarantee`

-- src:351 | 32 Constitutional documents to be provided to members
-- src:352 | (1) A company must, on request by any member, send to him the following documents—
-- src:353 | (a) an up-to-date copy of the company's articles;
-- src:354 | (b) a copy of any resolution or agreement relating to the company to which Chapter 3 applies (resolutions and agreements affecting a company's constitution) and that is for the time being in force;
-- src:355 | (c) a copy of any document required to be sent to the registrar under—
-- src:356 | (i) section 34(2) (notice where company's constitution altered by enactment), or
-- src:357 | (ii) section 35(2)(a) (notice where order of court or other authority alters company's constitution);
-- src:358 | (d) a copy of any court order under section 899 (order sanctioning compromise or arrangement) or section 900 (order facilitating reconstruction or amalgamation);
-- src:359 | (da) a copy of any court order under section 901F (order sanctioning compromise or arrangement for company in financial difficulty) or section 901J (order facilitating reconstruction or amalgamation);
-- src:360 | (e) a copy of any court order under section 996 (protection of members against unfair prejudice: powers of the court) that alters the company's constitution;
-- src:361 | (f) a copy of the company's current certificate of incorporation, and of any past certificates of incorporation;
-- src:362 | (g) in the case of a company with a share capital, a current statement of capital;
-- src:363 | (h) in the case of a company limited by guarantee, a copy of the statement of guarantee.
@ref s 32(1) Constitutional documents to be provided to members: on request by a member (src:351-363)
GIVEN `s 112 the person making the request is a member of the company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 32(1) the company must send the documents to the person on request` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 112 the person making the request is a member of the company`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A company must, on request by any member, send to him the following documents" (the duty arises only on request by a member, ruling of 2026-11-05 (b) and (c))
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "member" is defined in s 112

@ref s 32(1) Constitutional documents to be provided to members: the documents (src:353-363)
GIVEN c IS A `Company profile`
      `a resolution or agreement to which Chapter 3 applies is for the time being in force` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a document has been required to be sent to the registrar under section 34(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a document has been required to be sent to the registrar under section 35(2)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is a court order under section 899 or 900` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is a court order under section 901F or 901J` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is a court order under section 996 that alters the company's constitution` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A LIST OF `s 32(1) document the company must send`
`s 32(1) the documents the company must send to the member` MEANS
    concat (LIST articles, resolutions, under34, under35, order899, order901, order996, certificates, capital, guarantee)
    WHERE
        articles MEANS LIST `s 32(1)(a) an up-to-date copy of the company's articles`
        resolutions MEANS IF `a resolution or agreement to which Chapter 3 applies is for the time being in force` THEN LIST `s 32(1)(b) a copy of a resolution or agreement to which Chapter 3 applies that is for the time being in force` ELSE EMPTY
        under34 MEANS IF `a document has been required to be sent to the registrar under section 34(2)` THEN LIST `s 32(1)(c)(i) a copy of a document sent to the registrar under section 34(2)` ELSE EMPTY
        under35 MEANS IF `a document has been required to be sent to the registrar under section 35(2)(a)` THEN LIST `s 32(1)(c)(ii) a copy of a document sent to the registrar under section 35(2)(a)` ELSE EMPTY
        order899 MEANS IF `there is a court order under section 899 or 900` THEN LIST `s 32(1)(d) a copy of a court order under section 899 or 900` ELSE EMPTY
        order901 MEANS IF `there is a court order under section 901F or 901J` THEN LIST `s 32(1)(da) a copy of a court order under section 901F or 901J` ELSE EMPTY
        order996 MEANS IF `there is a court order under section 996 that alters the company's constitution` THEN LIST `s 32(1)(e) a copy of a court order under section 996 that alters the company's constitution` ELSE EMPTY
        certificates MEANS LIST `s 32(1)(f) a copy of the company's current certificate of incorporation, and of any past certificates`
        capital MEANS IF c's `a share capital` THEN LIST `s 32(1)(g) a current statement of capital` ELSE EMPTY
        guarantee MEANS IF `s 3(3) the company is limited by guarantee` (c's `liability of the members`) EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN LIST `s 32(1)(h) a copy of the statement of guarantee` ELSE EMPTY
    -- Each conditional document is listed only where the text's own condition holds ("a copy of any ...", "in the case of a company with a share capital", "in the case of a company limited by guarantee"); an absent one is the text's no for that document.

DECLARE `s 32(1) action` IS ONE OF
    `s 32(1) send the member the documents listed`

@ref s 32(1) Constitutional documents to be provided to members: the company's duty (src:352-352)
`s 32(1) the company's duty` MEANS
    PARTY Company
    MUST `s 32(1) send the member the documents listed`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company BECAUSE "the company did not send the member, on request, the documents listed in section 32(1)"

DECLARE `s 32(2)(c) statement for a class of shares` HAS
    `states the prescribed particulars of the rights attached to the shares` IS A BOOLEAN
    `states the total number of shares of that class` IS A BOOLEAN
    `states the aggregate nominal value of shares of that class` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:364 | (2) The statement of capital required by subsection (1)(g) is a statement of—
-- src:365 | (a) the total number of shares of the company,
-- src:366 | (b) the aggregate nominal value of those shares,
-- src:367 | (ba) the aggregate amount (if any) unpaid on those shares (whether on account of their nominal value or by way of premium), and
-- src:368 | (c) for each class of shares—
-- src:369 | (i) prescribed particulars of the rights attached to the shares,
-- src:370 | (ii) the total number of shares of that class, ...
-- src:371 | (iii) the aggregate nominal value of shares of that class, and
-- src:372 | (d) . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .
@ref s 32(2) Constitutional documents to be provided to members: the statement of capital (src:364-372)
GIVEN `the statement states the total number of shares of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement states the aggregate nominal value of those shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement states the aggregate amount (if any) unpaid on those shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statements for each class of shares` IS A LIST OF `s 32(2)(c) statement for a class of shares`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 32(2) the document is the statement of capital required by subsection (1)(g)` MEANS
    IF       `the statement states the total number of shares of the company`
         AND `the statement states the aggregate nominal value of those shares`
         AND `the statement states the aggregate amount (if any) unpaid on those shares`
         AND all (GIVEN c YIELD     c's `states the prescribed particulars of the rights attached to the shares`
                                AND c's `states the total number of shares of that class`
                                AND c's `states the aggregate nominal value of shares of that class`)
                 `the statements for each class of shares`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The statement of capital required by subsection (1)(g) is a statement of— (a) ..., (b) ..., (ba) ..., and (c) for each class of shares— (i) ..., (ii) ..., (iii) ..." (paragraph (d) is blank in this text)

-- src:373 | (3) If a company makes default in complying with this section, an offence is committed by every officer of the company who is in default.
@ref s 32(3) Constitutional documents to be provided to members: offence (src:373-373)
GIVEN `the company makes default in complying with section 32` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 1121 the officer is in default` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 32(3) the officer of the company commits an offence` MEANS
    IF NOT `the company makes default in complying with section 32`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a company makes default in complying with this section, an offence is committed by every officer of the company who is in default" (a failed "if" read as the text's no, marginal reading (a))
    ELSE CONSIDER `s 1121 the officer is in default`
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the offence is committed by "every officer of the company who is in default" and the text is silent on an officer who is not
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether an officer is in default is s 1121's answer

-- src:374 | (4) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding level 3 on the standard scale.
@ref s 32(4) Constitutional documents to be provided to members: the penalty (src:374-374)
`s 32(4) the penalty` MEANS Penalty WITH
    `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction`
    `imprisonment not exceeding` IS NOTHING
    `fine not exceeding` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 1)
    `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS NOTHING
    `imprisonment and fine together` IS FALSE

@ref s 32(4) Constitutional documents to be provided to members: the most the person can be fined (src:374-374)
GIVEN `level 3 on the standard scale, in pounds` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 32(4) the most the person can be fined on summary conviction, in pounds` MEANS
    `level 3 on the standard scale, in pounds`

-- ---- s 33: Effect of company's constitution --------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:375 | 33 Effect of company's constitution
-- src:376 | (1) The provisions of a company's constitution bind the company and its members to the same extent as if there were covenants on the part of the company and of each member to observe those provisions.
@ref s 33(1) Effect of company's constitution: it binds the company and its members (src:375-376)
GIVEN party IS A Party
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 33(1) the provisions of the constitution bind the party as if there were covenants` MEANS
    CONSIDER party
    WHEN Company THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN Member THEN JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "bind the company and its members"

-- src:377 | (2) Money payable by a member to the company under its constitution is a debt due from him to the company.
-- src:378 | In England and Wales and Northern Ireland it is of the nature of an ordinary contract debt.
@ref s 33(2) Effect of company's constitution: money payable by a member is a debt (src:377-378)
GIVEN `the money is payable by a member to the company under its constitution` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 33(2) the money is a debt due from the member to the company` MEANS
    IF `the money is payable by a member to the company under its constitution`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Money payable by a member to the company under its constitution is a debt due from him to the company"

@ref s 33(2) Effect of company's constitution: the nature of the debt (src:378-378)
GIVEN place IS A `Place of registration`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 33(2) the debt is of the nature of an ordinary contract debt` MEANS
    CONSIDER place
    WHEN `England and Wales` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `Northern Ireland` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `Scotland` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In England and Wales and Northern Ireland it is of the nature of an ordinary contract debt"

-- ---- s 34: Notice to registrar where company's constitution altered by enactment ------------------------

-- src:379 | 34 Notice to registrar where company's constitution altered by enactment
-- src:380 | (1) This section applies where a company's constitution is altered by an enactment, other than an enactment amending the general law.
@ref s 34(1) Notice where constitution altered by enactment: when the section applies (src:379-380)
GIVEN `the company's constitution is altered by an enactment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the enactment is an enactment amending the general law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 34(1) this section applies` MEANS
    IF `the company's constitution is altered by an enactment` AND (NOT `the enactment is an enactment amending the general law`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies where a company's constitution is altered by an enactment, other than an enactment amending the general law"

-- src:381 | (2) The company must give notice of the alteration to the registrar, specifying the enactment, not later than 15 days after the enactment comes into force.
-- src:382 | In the case of a special enactment the notice must be accompanied by a copy of the enactment.
-- src:383 | (3) If the enactment amends—
-- src:384 | (a) the company's articles, or
-- src:385 | (b) a resolution or agreement to which Chapter 3 applies (resolutions and agreements affecting a company's constitution),
-- src:386 | the notice must be accompanied by a copy of the company's articles, or the resolution or agreement in question, as amended.
@ref s 34(2) Notice where constitution altered by enactment: not later than 15 days after the enactment comes into force (src:381-386)
GIVEN `the date the enactment comes into force` IS A DATE
      `the date the notice is given to the registrar` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 34(2) the notice was given in time` MEANS
    IF `the date the notice is given to the registrar` AT MOST (`the date the enactment comes into force` PLUS 15)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The company must give notice of the alteration to the registrar, specifying the enactment, not later than 15 days after the enactment comes into force" (a period the text fixes in its own words, ruling of 2026-11-05 (a))

DECLARE `s 34 document that must accompany the notice` IS ONE OF
    `s 34(2) a copy of the special enactment`
    `s 34(3) a copy of the company's articles as amended`
    `s 34(3) a copy of the resolution or agreement as amended`

@ref s 34(2) Notice where constitution altered by enactment: documents that accompany the notice (src:382-386)
GIVEN `the enactment is a special enactment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the enactment amends the company's articles` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the enactment amends a resolution or agreement to which Chapter 3 applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A LIST OF `s 34 document that must accompany the notice`
`s 34(2) and (3) the documents that must accompany the notice` MEANS
    concat (LIST enactment, articles, resolution)
    WHERE
        enactment MEANS IF `the enactment is a special enactment` THEN LIST `s 34(2) a copy of the special enactment` ELSE EMPTY
        articles MEANS IF `the enactment amends the company's articles` THEN LIST `s 34(3) a copy of the company's articles as amended` ELSE EMPTY
        resolution MEANS IF `the enactment amends a resolution or agreement to which Chapter 3 applies` THEN LIST `s 34(3) a copy of the resolution or agreement as amended` ELSE EMPTY
    -- A document is listed only where the text's own condition holds ("In the case of a special enactment", "If the enactment amends"); an absent one is the text's no for that document.

-- src:387 | (4) A “special enactment” means an enactment that is not a public general enactment, and includes—
-- src:388 | (a) an Act for confirming a provisional order,
-- src:389 | (b) any provision of a public general Act in relation to the passing of which any of the standing orders of the House of Lords or the House of Commons relating to Private Business applied, or
-- src:390 | (c) any enactment to the extent that it is incorporated in or applied for the purposes of a special enactment.
@ref s 34(4) Notice where constitution altered by enactment: "special enactment" (src:387-390)
GIVEN `the enactment is a public general enactment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the enactment is an Act for confirming a provisional order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the enactment is a provision of a public general Act in relation to the passing of which any of the standing orders of the House of Lords or the House of Commons relating to Private Business applied` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the enactment is an enactment to the extent that it is incorporated in or applied for the purposes of a special enactment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 34(4) the enactment is a special enactment` MEANS
    IF `the enactment is an Act for confirming a provisional order` OR `the enactment is a provision of a public general Act in relation to the passing of which any of the standing orders of the House of Lords or the House of Commons relating to Private Business applied` OR `the enactment is an enactment to the extent that it is incorporated in or applied for the purposes of a special enactment`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF NOT `the enactment is a public general enactment`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A “special enactment” means an enactment that is not a public general enactment, and includes— (a) ..., (b) ..., or (c) ..."

DECLARE `s 34 action` IS ONE OF
    `s 34(2) give the registrar notice of the alteration, specifying the enactment`

-- src:381 | (2) The company must give notice of the alteration to the registrar, specifying the enactment, not later than 15 days after the enactment comes into force.
@ref s 34(2) Notice where constitution altered by enactment: the company's duty, in days (src:381-381)
`s 34(2) the company's duty` MEANS
    PARTY Company
    MUST `s 34(2) give the registrar notice of the alteration, specifying the enactment`
    WITHIN 15 -- days, counted from the day the enactment comes into force
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company BECAUSE "the company did not give the registrar notice of the alteration within 15 days after the enactment came into force"

-- src:391 | (5) If a company fails to comply with this section an offence is committed by—
-- src:392 | (a) the company, and
-- src:393 | (b) every officer of the company who is in default.
@ref s 34(5) Notice where constitution altered by enactment: offence by the company (src:391-393)
GIVEN `the company fails to comply with section 34` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 34(5)(a) the company commits an offence` MEANS
    IF `the company fails to comply with section 34`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a company fails to comply with this section an offence is committed by— (a) the company" (a failed "if" read as the text's no, marginal reading (a))

@ref s 34(5) Notice where constitution altered by enactment: offence by an officer in default (src:391-393)
GIVEN `the company fails to comply with section 34` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 1121 the officer is in default` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 34(5)(b) the officer of the company commits an offence` MEANS
    IF NOT `the company fails to comply with section 34`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a company fails to comply with this section an offence is committed by— ... (b) every officer of the company who is in default" (a failed "if" read as the text's no, marginal reading (a))
    ELSE CONSIDER `s 1121 the officer is in default`
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the offence is committed by "every officer of the company who is in default" and the text is silent on an officer who is not
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether an officer is in default is s 1121's answer

-- src:394 | (6) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding level 3 on the standard scale and, for continued contravention, a daily default fine not exceeding one-tenth of level 3 on the standard scale.
@ref s 34(6) Notice where constitution altered by enactment: the penalty (src:394-394)
`s 34(6) the penalty` MEANS Penalty WITH
    `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction`
    `imprisonment not exceeding` IS NOTHING
    `fine not exceeding` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 1)
    `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 0.1)
    `imprisonment and fine together` IS FALSE

@ref s 34(6) Notice where constitution altered by enactment: the most the person can be fined (src:394-394)
GIVEN `level 3 on the standard scale, in pounds` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 34(6) the most the person can be fined on summary conviction, in pounds` MEANS
    `level 3 on the standard scale, in pounds`

@ref s 34(6) Notice where constitution altered by enactment: the most the daily default fine can be (src:394-394)
GIVEN `level 3 on the standard scale, in pounds` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 34(6) the most the daily default fine can be for each day of continued contravention, in pounds` MEANS
    `level 3 on the standard scale, in pounds` TIMES 0.1

-- ---- s 35: Notice to registrar where company's constitution altered by order ---------------------------

-- src:407 | (5) This section does not apply where provision is made by another enactment for the delivery to the registrar of a copy of the order in question.
@ref s 35(5) Notice where constitution altered by order: another enactment provides for delivery (src:407-407)
GIVEN `another enactment makes provision for the delivery to the registrar of a copy of the order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 35(5) this section applies` MEANS
    IF `another enactment makes provision for the delivery to the registrar of a copy of the order`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section does not apply where provision is made by another enactment for the delivery to the registrar of a copy of the order in question"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the flat negative names only a case where another enactment makes provision for delivery of the order

-- src:395 | 35 Notice to registrar where company's constitution altered by order
-- src:396 | (1) Where a company's constitution is altered by an order of a court or other authority, the company must give notice to the registrar of the alteration not later than 15 days after the alteration takes effect.
@ref s 35(1) Notice where constitution altered by order: not later than 15 days after the alteration takes effect (src:395-396)
GIVEN `the company's constitution is altered by an order of a court or other authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the answer under s 35(5) that this section applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 35(1) the company must give notice to the registrar of the alteration` MEANS
    IF NOT `the company's constitution is altered by an order of a court or other authority`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a company's constitution is altered by an order of a court or other authority, the company must give notice to the registrar of the alteration" (the duty arises only where, ruling of 2026-11-05 (b))
    ELSE CONSIDER `the answer under s 35(5) that this section applies`
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section does not apply where provision is made by another enactment for the delivery to the registrar of a copy of the order in question"
         OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

@ref s 35(1) Notice where constitution altered by order: within 15 days (src:396-396)
GIVEN `the date the alteration takes effect` IS A DATE
      `the date the notice is given to the registrar` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 35(1) the notice was given in time` MEANS
    IF `the date the notice is given to the registrar` AT MOST (`the date the alteration takes effect` PLUS 15)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the company must give notice to the registrar of the alteration not later than 15 days after the alteration takes effect" (a period the text fixes in its own words, ruling of 2026-11-05 (a))

DECLARE `s 35 document that must accompany the notice` IS ONE OF
    `s 35(2)(a) a copy of the order`
    `s 35(2)(b)(i) a copy of the company's articles as amended`
    `s 35(2)(b)(ii) a copy of the resolution or agreement as amended`

-- src:397 | (2) The notice must be accompanied by—
-- src:398 | (a) a copy of the order, and
-- src:399 | (b) if the order amends—
-- src:400 | (i) the company's articles, or
-- src:401 | (ii) a resolution or agreement to which Chapter 3 applies (resolutions and agreements affecting the company's constitution),
-- src:402 | a copy of the company's articles, or the resolution or agreement in question, as amended.
@ref s 35(2) Notice where constitution altered by order: documents that accompany the notice (src:397-402)
GIVEN `the order amends the company's articles` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the order amends a resolution or agreement to which Chapter 3 applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A LIST OF `s 35 document that must accompany the notice`
`s 35(2) the documents that must accompany the notice` MEANS
    concat (LIST order, articles, resolution)
    WHERE
        order MEANS LIST `s 35(2)(a) a copy of the order`
        articles MEANS IF `the order amends the company's articles` THEN LIST `s 35(2)(b)(i) a copy of the company's articles as amended` ELSE EMPTY
        resolution MEANS IF `the order amends a resolution or agreement to which Chapter 3 applies` THEN LIST `s 35(2)(b)(ii) a copy of the resolution or agreement as amended` ELSE EMPTY
    -- The copy of the order is always listed ("The notice must be accompanied by— (a) a copy of the order"); each amended document only "if the order amends" it, and an absent one is the text's no for that document.

DECLARE `s 35 action` IS ONE OF
    `s 35(1) give the registrar notice of the alteration`

