-- ---- s 36: Documents to be incorporated in or accompany copies of articles issued by company ----------------

-- src:408 | 36 Documents to be incorporated in or accompany copies of articles issued by company
-- src:409 | (1) Every copy of a company's articles issued by the company must be accompanied by—
-- src:410 | (a) a copy of any resolution or agreement relating to the company to which Chapter 3 applies (resolutions and agreements affecting a company's constitution),
-- src:411 | (b) where the company has been required to give notice to the registrar under section 34(2) (notice where company's constitution altered by enactment), a statement that the enactment in question alters the effect of the company's constitution,
-- src:412 | (c) where the company's constitution is altered by a special enactment (see section 34(4)), a copy of the enactment, and
-- src:413 | (d) a copy of any order required to be sent to the registrar under section 35(2)(a) (order of court or other authority altering company's constitution).
-- src:414 | (2) This does not require the articles to be accompanied by a copy of a document or by a statement if—
-- src:415 | (a) the effect of the resolution, agreement, enactment or order (as the case may be) on the company's constitution has been incorporated into the articles by amendment, or
-- src:416 | (b) the resolution, agreement, enactment or order (as the case may be) is not for the time being in force.
@ref s 36(1) and (2) Documents to accompany copies of articles: the documents and when they are not required (src:408-416)
GIVEN `the document or statement is one that section 36(1)(a), (b), (c) or (d) describes` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the effect of the resolution, agreement, enactment or order on the company's constitution has been incorporated into the articles by amendment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the resolution, agreement, enactment or order is not for the time being in force` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 36(1) the document or statement must accompany the copy of the articles issued` MEANS
    IF NOT `the document or statement is one that section 36(1)(a), (b), (c) or (d) describes`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every copy of a company's articles issued by the company must be accompanied by— (a) ... (b) where ... (c) where ... (d) ..." (the duty arises only for the documents and statements listed, ruling of 2026-11-05 (b))
    ELSE IF `the effect of the resolution, agreement, enactment or order on the company's constitution has been incorporated into the articles by amendment` OR `the resolution, agreement, enactment or order is not for the time being in force`
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This does not require the articles to be accompanied by a copy of a document or by a statement if— (a) the effect of the resolution, agreement, enactment or order (as the case may be) on the company's constitution has been incorporated into the articles by amendment, or (b) the resolution, agreement, enactment or order (as the case may be) is not for the time being in force"
         ELSE JUST TRUE

DECLARE `s 36(1) action` IS ONE OF
    `s 36(1) accompany the copy of the articles with the documents and statements required`

@ref s 36(1) Documents to accompany copies of articles: the company's duty on each copy (src:409-409)
`s 36(1) the company's duty on each copy issued` MEANS
    PARTY Company
    MUST `s 36(1) accompany the copy of the articles with the documents and statements required`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company BECAUSE "a copy of the articles was issued without the documents and statements that must accompany it"

